    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1400">

                <pb facs="1131" n="1121" xml:id="pg1121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.7141/11–3049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clubb</hi>)<anchor n="49" xml:id="d1400-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-08T18:00:00-05:00">December 8, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>887. Urtel 2155 Nov 30. Because of deadline suggest you inform local Commie auths
                    Peiping properties acquired by “Final protocol for the settlement of the
                    disturbances of 1900” concluded at Peking, Sept 7, 1901 (Art. VII)<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d1400-f2"/> and rights thereto confirmed by “Treaty between the
                    United States of America and the Republic of China for the relinquishment of
                    extraterritorial rights in China and the regulation of related matters”, which
                    was signed at Washington Jan 11, 1943 and entered into force May 20, 1943 (Art.
                        II).<anchor n="51" xml:id="d1400-f3"/> Suggest you concert with
                    colleagues.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1400-f1" n="49" type="source" xml:id="d1400-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Embassy at Nanking as No. 1282.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1400-f2" n="50" xml:id="d1400-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1901#pg_312">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Appendix, 1901, Affairs in
                        China, pp. 312</ref>, <ref target="frus1901#pg_316">316</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1400-f3" n="51" xml:id="d1400-f3-content">
                <p>Department of State Treaty Series No. 984, or 57 Stat. (pt. 2) 767, 768.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
